  "rawText": "Vi.\n\nVil.\n\nVII.\n\n4. Past president of the Brunswick County Unit of the N.C. Teachers Association.\nSi Host Teacher-Trainer for undergraduates students from the country of Nigeria.\nRELIGIOUS AFFILIATIONS\n\nii. Member of the Friendship Baptist Church, in Southport, N.C.\n\n2. Church treasurer for 41 years.\n3. Chairman of Trustee Board for 40 years.\n4. Chairman of Trustee-Board of the Ocean View Missionary Baptist Association for 24 years.\n\n< A Director of the Southport-Oak-Island Inter-Church Fellowship.\n\nCOMMUNITY SERVICE\n\ni. Life member of the NAACP and a member of the Education Committee of the Southport\nArea Branch.\n\n2. Chairman of the Advisory Committee of the Southport Elementary School.\n\n3. Member of the Brunswick County Citizens Committee.\n\n4. Retired chairman of the Brunswick County Resources Commission.\n5. Charter Director of the Southport-Oak Island Chamber of Commerce.\n6. Member of Southport Economic Development Commission.\n\ni, A Director of the Brunswick County Adult Care, Inc.\n\n8. A Director of the Southport Maritime Museum.\n\n9. A number of awards and citations have been awarded as a well known educator, religious\nleader, a successful business man and a highly respected citizen of the community.\n\nBASIC VALUES\n\n1. | believe each individual was sent to the world for a definite purpose and with a specific\ntalent to share. Therefore, it becomes each person’s responsibility to recognize that\npurpose, discover and develop his talent and to use it to the fullest extent in whatever area",
  "cleanedText": "Vi.\n\nVil.\n\nVII.\n\n4. Past president of the Brunswick County Unit of the N.C. Teachers Association.\nSi Host Teacher-Trainer for undergraduates students from the country of Nigeria.\nRELIGIOUS AFFILIATIONS\n\nii. Member of the Friendship Baptist Church, in Southport, N.C.\n\n2. Church treasurer for 41 years.\n3. Chairman of Trustee Board for 40 years.\n4. Chairman of Trustee-Board of the Ocean View Missionary Baptist Association for 24 years.\n\n< A Director of the Southport-Oak-Island Inter-Church Fellowship.\n\nCOMMUNITY SERVICE\n\ni. Life member of the NAACP and a member of the Education Committee of the Southport\nArea Branch.\n\n2. Chairman of the Advisory Committee of the Southport Elementary School.\n\n3. Member of the Brunswick County Citizens Committee.\n\n4. Retired chairman of the Brunswick County Resources Commission.\n5. Charter Director of the Southport-Oak Island Chamber of Commerce.\n6. Member of Southport Economic Development Commission.\n\ni, A Director of the Brunswick County Adult Care, Inc.\n\n8. A Director of the Southport Maritime Museum.\n\n9. A number of awards and citations have been awarded as a well known educator, religious\nleader, a successful business man and a highly respected citizen of the community.\n\nBASIC VALUES\n\n1. I believe each individual was sent to the world for a definite purpose and with a specific\ntalent to share. Therefore, it becomes each person’s responsibility to recognize that\npurpose, discover and develop his talent and to use it to the fullest extent in whatever area",
